  "name": "Question 4",
  "problem": "Given the statement\n\n$$\nP:3\\text{\u00a0is smaller than\u00a0}5\n$$\n\n \nwhich of the following represents $\u00acP?$",
  "worked_solution": "The symbol \"$\u00ac$\" represents negation. So, our task is to negate the given sentence. \n\nTo negate our plain English sentence, we place the words \"It is not true that\" in front of it. This gives the following:\n\n$$\n\u00acP:\\text{It is not true that\u00a0}3\\text{\u00a0is smaller than\u00a0}5.\n$$\n\n \n\nIn other words, $3$ is *not* smaller than $5.$ Therefore, $\u00acP$ means the following:\n\n$$\n\u00acP:3\\text{\u00a0is\u00a0}\\text{not}\\text{\u00a0smaller than\u00a0}5.\n$$\n\n \n\nNote that $P$ is **true,** while $\u00acP$ is **false.**",
